00:06:39.890 --> 00:06:44.650
A fun song that was sadly cut from the movie
was a big musical number where Branch and

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:46.933
Hickory sang an ode to Poppy who they called
the "Queen of Pop".

00:06:46.933 --> 00:06:52.710
♪ Following the Queen of Pop
Knowing that you won't give up ♪

00:06:52.710 --> 00:07:00.520
This deleted song was storyboarded by DreamWorks
artist Jeremy Bernstein and is sung in a country-pop

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:03.300
crossover style.

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:06.950
♪ We're just a pair of fools
Who'll do anything for you ♪

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:11.610
A little bit of this original scene was kept
in the final movie when Hickory sings a short

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:16.460
country song to Branch accompanied by singing
river reeds, though in the final version,

00:07:16.460 --> 00:07:19.820
the song he sings is Patsy Cline's I Fall
to Pieces.

00:07:19.820 --> 00:07:24.610
The giant river eel-like creatures that swim
under the boat in this deleted scene also

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:29.780
appeared in unused Trolls World Tour concept
art of the trolls telling each other ghost

00:07:29.780 --> 00:07:30.780
stories.

00:07:30.780 --> 00:07:35.820
A great deleted scene with the movie's antagonist
sees Barb rocking up at an old diner in her

00:07:35.820 --> 00:07:38.660
"World Destruction Tour" Anglerbus.

00:07:38.660 --> 00:07:43.030
Inside the diner are groups of trolls whose
musical styles are no longer very popular

00:07:43.030 --> 00:07:46.110
so they're sitting around feeling sorry for
themselves.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:49.310
"Singing your heart out and nobody cares.

00:07:49.310 --> 00:07:52.130
Not fun, is it?

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:55.460
You've all heard of pop music?

00:07:55.460 --> 00:08:00.370
They think they're so great because they're
'popular'.

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:03.440
But you guys are going to help me change that.

00:08:03.440 --> 00:08:06.300
Little Miss Polka.

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:09.169
The Mariachi Sisters.

00:08:09.169 --> 00:08:10.820
The Barbershop Boys.

00:08:10.820 --> 00:08:14.190
And Jax, the Smooth Jazzer."

00:08:14.190 --> 00:08:15.190
"Hey babe."

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:19.850
The Smooth Jazz troll then almost hypnotises
Barb with his laid-back tunes.

00:08:19.850 --> 00:08:20.850
"That's enough!

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:23.010
Save it for Queen Poppy."

00:08:23.010 --> 00:08:26.830
Which, of course, he does later in the actual
movie with Poppy and Branch.

00:08:26.830 --> 00:08:30.230
"I can't feel my face."

00:08:30.230 --> 00:08:34.539
Barb's reward for Poppy's capture is also
a little different in this cut version:

00:08:34.539 --> 00:08:40.279
"Whoever brings me Queen Poppy and her string,
will be the opening act on my World Destruction

00:08:40.279 --> 00:08:41.279
Tour!"

00:08:41.279 --> 00:08:45.880
Whereas of that, in the actual movie, Barb
offers the winning bounty hunters a tiny refuge

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:46.880
for their own music.

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:47.880
"I don't know.

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:48.880
It looks pretty tiny."

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:49.880
"You want it or not?"

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:53.990
The sneaky Yodellers also get a different
introduction in this deleted scene:

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:59.000
"If you really want the job done right,
you need a couple of Yodellers.

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:00.000
Ya.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.190
We will find this Queen Poppy..
and we will stop at nothing."

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:10.570
The Yodeller's true identity is still kept
a secret with Hickory and Dickory hiding behind

00:09:10.570 --> 00:09:12.570
a pair of beer glasses.

00:09:12.570 --> 00:09:16.560
What's also interesting about this deleted
scene is that, instead of Barb using a group

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:20.140
of bounty hunters that only represented less
popular music,

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:24.960
in the final film, DreamWorks also included
K-Pop and Reggaeton trolls because they wanted

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:30.120
to make sure there was more musical diversity
in the film and they're two very popular genres.

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:35.440
In an alternate version of the movie, Poppy
and co were going to meet Hickory before they

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:38.480
arrived at Lonesome Flats, home of the Country
Trolls.

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:40.130
"See a troll.

00:09:40.130 --> 00:09:41.130
Just like us."

00:09:41.130 --> 00:09:42.170
"I say we steer clear."

00:09:42.170 --> 00:09:46.080
"Now Branch we're out here to build bridges.

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:48.720
If we steer clear, how will we make new friends?"

00:09:48.720 --> 00:09:50.760
"Yeah, more like making new enemies."

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:55.730
But despite Poppy's enthusiasm, the encounter
with Hickory has a spaghetti western-type

00:09:55.730 --> 00:09:58.260
vibe as they all eye each other up suspiciously.

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:00.830
"Hi there, I'm Queen Poppy."

00:10:00.830 --> 00:10:01.860
"Queen Poppy?"

00:10:01.860 --> 00:10:05.540
"Uh huh, of the Pop Trolls."

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:06.570
"Ah!"

00:10:06.570 --> 00:10:08.649
"Oh oh!"

00:10:08.649 --> 00:10:09.690
"Yippee-ki-yay."

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:12.810
"Only two legs.

00:10:12.810 --> 00:10:16.980
Thought I'd seen everything."

00:10:16.980 --> 00:10:21.100
Hickory's comments about Poppy only having
two legs and not four like him

00:10:21.100 --> 00:10:26.120
are a hint to his secret identity as he's
also really just a two-legged Yodeller troll

00:10:26.120 --> 00:10:28.820
pretending to be a four-legged Country Troll.

00:10:28.820 --> 00:10:33.090
To keep up his disguise, Hickory continues
to act distrustful around Poppy.

00:10:33.090 --> 00:10:35.160
"Where do you tumbleweeds come from?

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:37.570
I don't take kindly to being ambushed."

00:10:37.570 --> 00:10:38.870
"Oh, no, no, no, no, no.

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:40.490
We come in peace.

00:10:40.490 --> 00:10:41.720
In fact, er..

00:10:41.720 --> 00:10:45.510
I'd like to make a peace offering of...
drumroll please...

00:10:45.510 --> 00:10:48.060
cotton candy?"

00:10:48.060 --> 00:10:53.120
Remember, that cotton candy is what Poppy
was carrying on Sheila B as a plan to make

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:55.029
friends with Barb in the final film.

00:10:55.029 --> 00:10:59.730
"I hope you didn't eat all the cotton candy,
because Barb is gonna love it.

00:10:59.730 --> 00:11:05.020
And Poppy's sugary offering finally sweetens
up Hickory when he tries it.

00:11:05.020 --> 00:11:06.450
"Cotton...

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:07.890
Candy?

00:11:07.890 --> 00:11:10.760
Uh huh!

00:11:10.760 --> 00:11:17.390
Well howdy, that's a right tasty treat!

00:11:17.390 --> 00:11:18.390
Name's Hickory.

00:11:18.390 --> 00:11:19.480
What can I do you for?"

00:11:19.480 --> 00:11:23.899
Another song early in the movie that ended
up getting cut took place on the Sheila B

00:11:23.899 --> 00:11:28.130
balloon and was going to show Poppy revealing
her plan for saving the Troll kingdom.

00:11:28.130 --> 00:11:30.399
"We're going to find other trolls.

00:11:30.399 --> 00:11:34.330
All we have to do is come together and embrace
our sameness."

00:11:34.330 --> 00:11:35.690
"Woo hoo!

00:11:35.690 --> 00:11:37.060
Yes Poppy!"

00:11:37.060 --> 00:11:41.960
The original scene for this was storyboarded
by DreamWorks artist Jon Magram and features

00:11:41.960 --> 00:11:45.670
Poppy singing to the tune of "Can You Feel
It" by The Jacksons.

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:50.920
It's a fun and zany musical number which shows
how Poppy thinks the solution to Barb's attempt

00:11:50.920 --> 00:11:56.700
to take over the world with Rock is to shower
Pop Music uniformity over everyone instead.

00:11:56.700 --> 00:12:01.750
The cut scene mixes a dream-like quality with
the look of Poppy's scrap-booking and shows

00:12:01.750 --> 00:12:06.529
her blanketing the Troll kingdom with pop
music glitter, sparkles and hearts.

00:12:06.529 --> 00:12:11.990
Her eyes and mouth blast out multi-coloured
rays of light over the other trolls, turning

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:16.290
their eyes into hearts and them into a string
of happy pop troll puppets.

00:12:16.290 --> 00:12:21.100
Branch, who we know is resistant to some of
Poppy's excessive exuberance, uses one of

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:25.540
his pointy sticks and a rock to smash one
of the hearts Poppy is spreading everywhere,

00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:30.149
only for her to stick it back on him where
it expands and smothers him.

00:12:30.149 --> 00:12:35.420
The deleted song reveals that Poppy's blind
to just how oppressive her ideas really are

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:40.420
and shows some unflattering parallels between
her and Barb in the way Poppy turns other

00:12:40.420 --> 00:12:45.810
trolls into Pop Music zombies, just as Barb
later turns them into Rock Music zombies.

00:12:45.810 --> 00:12:50.100
In the end, the filmmakers decided the song
was slowing down the story too much, so it

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:51.100
was cut.

00:12:51.100 --> 00:12:55.550
A small deleted scene at the beginning of
the movie saw Cooper having a conversation

00:12:55.550 --> 00:13:00.020
with a reflection of himself about whether
he thought he was really from one of the other

00:13:00.020 --> 00:13:01.020
Troll tribes.

00:13:01.020 --> 00:13:02.020
"Hey you.

00:13:02.020 --> 00:13:04.180
Do you think I'm one of these different kind
of trolls?

00:13:04.180 --> 00:13:06.190
Come on me, I'm just a reflection.

00:13:06.190 --> 00:13:08.450
You have to get on out there and find out.

00:13:08.450 --> 00:13:09.760
You're right us.

00:13:09.760 --> 00:13:13.250
I have to get out into this wide world and
find out for myself.

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:15.990
I can always count on you me.

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:16.990
Thanks.

00:13:16.990 --> 00:13:19.270
That means a lot to me, us."

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:23.610
Although the scene's amusing and reminded
me a little of Disney's original Mary Poppins

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:28.360
movie, the word play is possibly a little
confusing which may be why it ended up being

00:13:28.360 --> 00:13:29.360
cut.

00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:33.670
However, a snippet of this idea was used in
the final film when Cooper's reflection talks

00:13:33.670 --> 00:13:36.430
back to him in a mirage.

00:13:36.430 --> 00:13:37.529
"I'm saved!"

00:13:37.529 --> 00:13:39.170
"Are you, now?

00:13:39.170 --> 00:13:43.540
Cause last I checked, I was a mirage."

00:13:43.540 --> 00:13:48.090
When Poppy and her entourage arrive at Symphonyville,
they meet Pennywhistle who tells them all

00:13:48.090 --> 00:13:52.100
about the destruction Barb and the Rock Trolls
wreaked on the Classical kingdom.

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:56.860
A deleted scene which was cut for time showed
more of what happened and revealed that Pennywhistle

00:13:56.860 --> 00:13:59.500
was actually Symphonyville's security guard.

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:04.110
In the scene, we see how the little tin whistle,
unfortunately, took a short break from her

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:06.490
post just before the Rock Trolls arrived.

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:10.730
Oh time for my union break.

00:14:10.730 --> 00:14:12.240
Yay!

00:14:12.240 --> 00:14:13.760
Ohh.

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:20.350
A nice little detail in this missing moment
is that we would have seen that Pennywhistle

00:14:20.350 --> 00:14:25.400
was a model citizen having repeatedly won
Symphonyville's "Employee of the Month" award.

00:14:25.400 --> 00:14:30.060
The deleted scene also showed a full-on battle
between the Classical and Rock Trolls with

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:32.060
the Classical Trolls almost winning.

00:14:32.060 --> 00:14:33.060
"Ha, ha, ha.

00:14:33.060 --> 00:14:34.060
Ow!

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:35.060
Hit in my eye."

00:14:35.060 --> 00:14:36.060
"We have the Classical string!"

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:37.060
"Oh dear."

00:14:37.060 --> 00:14:38.060
Another deleted trailer scene shows King Trollex
handing over the Techno String to Queen Barb.

00:14:38.060 --> 00:14:39.060
"I'm gonna unite the six strings and destroy
all music.

00:14:39.060 --> 00:14:40.060
Except for rock!

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:41.060
So I'm gonna need your string."

00:14:41.060 --> 00:14:42.060
And if you look carefully at this cut scene,
you'll see that it would have revealed that

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:43.060
the Techno String was held in Techno Beat
Drop Button,

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:44.060
as the middle blue string he normally has
on his head is now missing.

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:46.100
The scene might have been cut because Techno
Beat Drop Button appears at the end of the

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:47.100
movie with all his strings intact even after
all of the six strings have been destroyed.

00:14:47.100 --> 00:14:51.700
In the final film, when the Rock Trolls attack
Vibe City, the Funk Trolls ready themselves

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:52.700
for attack.

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:53.700
"Rock has arrived!"

00:14:53.700 --> 00:14:54.700
"It's on!

00:14:54.700 --> 00:14:55.700
Prepare for battle!"

00:14:55.700 --> 00:15:00.020
But the battle never takes place as the Rock
Trolls cut the power to Vibe City.

00:15:00.020 --> 00:15:04.529
However, concept art by Timothy Lamb shows
that originally DreamWorks planned to have

00:15:04.529 --> 00:15:08.260
a proper music battle between the Funk Trolls
and the Rock Trolls.

00:15:08.260 --> 00:15:12.770
As the fight between the Classical and Rock
Trolls was also deleted, we never got to see

00:15:12.770 --> 00:15:17.779
any actual battles between the tribes, and
instead in the final movie Barb and her gang

00:15:17.779 --> 00:15:21.459
seem to quickly overwhelm any resistance they
encounter.

00:15:21.459 --> 00:15:26.420
Another cut moment revealed in concept art
shows that when Poppy and co were imprisoned

00:15:26.420 --> 00:15:31.010
in Lonesome Flats, they were going to discover
the skeleton remains of previous prisoners

00:15:31.010 --> 00:15:32.519
inside their jail.

00:15:32.519 --> 00:15:37.390
This morbid joke would have fit with the Country
Trolls' somewhat sad and macabre take on life

00:15:37.390 --> 00:15:39.830
that we heard in the song "Born To Die".

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:44.700
After Hickory busts Poppy and the gang out
of jail, they end up running off the edge

00:15:44.700 --> 00:15:48.390
of a canyon into the river below as they flee
from the Country Trolls.

00:15:48.390 --> 00:15:53.010
However, what we didn't get to see in the
final version was this scene of them almost

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:55.120
drowning in the river of yarn.

00:15:55.120 --> 00:16:00.180
In the final movie, we just see Poppy and
Branch washed up on the river bank instead.

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:04.769
The only remnant of this original idea which
did make it into the film is Dinkle's vision

00:16:04.769 --> 00:16:06.709
of ascending to heaven.

00:16:06.709 --> 00:16:08.490
"Welcome home."

00:16:08.490 --> 00:16:12.930
"Oh, Mr. Dinkles, you're alive.

00:16:12.930 --> 00:16:19.700
For a minute there, I thought you'd kicked
the bucket."

00:16:19.700 --> 00:16:20.700
[groans]

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:25.620
And more concept art reveals another cut scene
of Branch saving Poppy, pulling her out of

00:16:25.620 --> 00:16:26.620
the river.

00:16:26.620 --> 00:16:30.839
The purpose of this drawing was also to figure
out what the Trolls would look like when they're

00:16:30.839 --> 00:16:34.980
wet, because there isn't any real water in
the Trolls world as even the water in the

00:16:34.980 --> 00:16:38.170
river is designed to resemble shiny gossamer
fabric.

00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:42.890
In another deleted scene on the water, we
would have seen Cooper meeting a mysterious

00:16:42.890 --> 00:16:47.100
character called "Bridge Fisherman" as he
crossed the river on his quest to find his

00:16:47.100 --> 00:16:48.250
Troll tribe.

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:52.510
This furry-looking troll is quite different
from any other trolls in the movie

00:16:52.510 --> 00:16:58.160
and if you want to discover more deleted characters
from the film such as the K-Pop boy band,

00:16:58.160 --> 00:17:02.070
the Giant Funk Troll King, or the Classical
Cooper trolls,

00:17:02.070 --> 00:17:06.659
tap here to watch my Trolls World Tour Deleted
Characters video or follow the link in the

00:17:06.659 --> 00:17:07.659
video description.

00:17:07.659 --> 00:17:10.189
Link will be here as soon as it's ready.

00:17:10.189 --> 00:17:14.699
And if you love the amazing artwork by the
DreamWorks artists featured in this video,

00:17:14.699 --> 00:17:18.829
you can discover much more of it in The Art
of Trolls book and their Instagrams.

00:17:18.829 --> 00:17:21.589
There's links to those in the video description
below.

00:17:21.589 --> 00:17:26.499
So, do you wish any of these deleted scenes
or songs had been included in the movie?

00:17:26.499 --> 00:17:28.690
